<alcuin. carm. 53.1>	Curre viam, frater, angusto tramite pulchram,
<alcuin. carm. 53.2>	Quae te sub tectis domini deducat in aulam;
<alcuin. carm. 53.3>	Nec tibi forte pedes coeno sordente respargit,
<alcuin. carm. 53.4>	Nec tibi caeruleus crines infuderit imber;
<alcuin. carm. 53.5>	Nec vis ventorum turbat, nec grando procellis;
<alcuin. carm. 53.6>	Nec timor, ut tollant vestes, nec fauce latrones,
<alcuin. carm. 53.7>	Nec leo, nec tygris, ursus, aper ambo visuntur;
<alcuin. carm. 53.8>	Vel coluber, regulus, serpens prosternit euntem,
<alcuin. carm. 53.9>	Sed bene securus poteris percurrere stratam.
<alcuin. carm. 53.10>	Laus divina tibi resonet quapropter in ore,
<alcuin. carm. 53.11>	Utque pium placido Christum tu pectore porta:
<alcuin. carm. 53.12>	Ille tuos gressus, sensus et verba gubernet,
<alcuin. carm. 53.13>	Dux, via, rector, amor tibi sit, protector ubique
<alcuin. carm. 53.14>	Incolomem ducat te, teque reducat euntem.
